    "interpretation": "The retained no-actuation arm settles into a near-stationary supported regime where Rapier applies its force-derived velocity increment before the first measured constraint phase. The measured constraints then remove 99.953 percent of the independently projected zero-velocity gravity-kick energy at the terminal step, while endpoint mechanical energy changes by only 0.000000589 J and the residual grows by essentially the same projected amount. This localizes a real discrete force/constraint/position staging boundary in the observer. It does not prove that the whole active candidate residual has this cause, and the projection cannot be inserted as a correction because free fall and moving motion also require potential-energy staging to avoid double counting physical gravity work."
